#: ../../../deployment.md:1
msgid "Deployment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deployment.md:3
msgid "Zip files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deployment.md:8
msgid ""
"To make it easier to distribute, you can zip up your Python code into a zip "
"file. If you use UDFs, this will disable the automatic code reload, so this "
"is a feature meant for distribution, not development. In practice, this "
"means that when your code is inside a zip file, you'll have to click on re-"
"import to get any changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deployment.md:12
msgid ""
"If you name your zip file like your Excel file (but with `.zip` extension) "
"and place it in the same folder as your Excel workbook, xlwings will "
"automatically find it (similar to how it works with a single python file)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deployment.md:15
msgid ""
"If you want to use a different directory, make sure to add it to the "
"`PYTHONPATH` in your config (Ribbon or config file):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deployment.md:21
msgid "RunFrozenPython"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deployment.md:26
msgid ""
"You can use a freezer like PyInstaller, cx_Freeze, py2exe etc. to freeze "
"your Python module into an executable so that the recipient doesn't have to "
"install a full Python distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deployment.md:30
msgid "This does not work with UDFs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deployment.md:31
msgid ""
"Currently only available on Windows, but support for Mac should be easy to "
"add."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../deployment.md:32
msgid ""
"You need at least 0.15.2 to support arguments whereas the syntax changed in "
"0.15.6"
msgstr ""

